kcov-76bf685.patch -- upstream kcov commit 76bf685 ("bash-engine: Don't
print continuation lines of multi-line trace entries", SimonKagstrom/kcov
issue 464), backported onto the v43 tag that dockerfile/Dockerfile.test-tools
builds. Only the diff below is applied (`git apply` skips this header).

With BASH_XTRACEFD the trace pipe carries trace output only, so a line
with no `kcov@` marker is a piece of a trace record, not the script's own
stderr; v43 echoes every such line to kcov's stderr (base#1414).

diff --git a/src/engines/bash-engine.cc b/src/engines/bash-engine.cc
index 2f76e04..0d32dbb 100644
--- a/src/engines/bash-engine.cc
+++ b/src/engines/bash-engine.cc
@@ -288,7 +288,12 @@ public:
 		size_t kcovStr = cur.find("kcov@");
 		if (kcovStr == std::string::npos)
 		{
-			fprintf(stderr, "%s", cur.c_str());
+			// With BASH_XTRACEFD, the pipe only carries trace output. A line without
+			// a marker is part of a multi-line trace entry, or traced with a different
+			// PS4. Otherwise the pipe is also the script's stderr, and this may be the
+			// script's own output.
+			if (!m_bashSupportsXtraceFd)
+				fprintf(stderr, "%s", cur.c_str());
 			return true;
 		}
 		m_inputType = getInputType(cur);
